INT. MATTRESS SHOWROOM - DAY

A cavernous retail floor of identical beds under bright lights. Price tags like confetti. A banner: "NOTHING DOWN! EVERYTHING SOFT!"

CASSIUS BLACKWOOD-ADEYEMI, 40s, a sales manager in an ill-fitting suit, stands at a display bed holding a clipboard. Opposite him, MARIGOLD DUPONT-ASANTE, 30s, a regional auditor with a briefcase, stands with her arms folded.

CASSIUS
Welcome to Bedrock Mattress Gallery. May I interest you in a night of salvation?

MARIGOLD
I'm from corporate.

CASSIUS
(sagging)
Ah.

MARIGOLD
I'm here to audit your sales.

CASSIUS
Of course.

MARIGOLD
You're down sixty percent.

CASSIUS
It's a down market.

MARIGOLD
Mattresses are never down.

CASSIUS
They're flat, Marigold.

MARIGOLD
That is not funny.

CASSIUS
It's a little funny.

She walks the floor, scribbling. He trails her, wringing his hands.

MARIGOLD
Where is everyone?

CASSIUS
Lunch.

MARIGOLD
It's two p.m.

CASSIUS
Long lunch.

MARIGOLD
Cassius.

CASSIUS
Union.

MARIGOLD
You don't have a union.

CASSIUS
We have a book club.

MARIGOLD
That's not the same.

CASSIUS
They read a lot.

She stops at a display bed. Presses a hand to the mattress. It sighs. She pokes it. Pokes again.

MARIGOLD
This model is called the "Cloud Nine"?

CASSIUS
Yes.

MARIGOLD
It's lumpy.

CASSIUS
It's organic.

She sits on the edge. Tests it. Lies back. Her eyes drift shut.

MARIGOLD
(softly)
Oh.

CASSIUS
Yes.

MARIGOLD
Oh, no.

CASSIUS
Corporate always says that.

MARIGOLD
This is the best mattress I've ever laid on.

CASSIUS
Why do you think nobody's at lunch?

She sits up slowly. Cassius gestures behind her. Along the back wall, twelve employees lie on twelve mattresses, hands folded on their chests, eyes closed, perfectly still. A soft, collective snore rises.

Marigold looks at them. Looks at her clipboard. Looks at Cassius. Slowly, she lowers the clipboard, takes off her shoes, and sets them neatly on the floor. Then she lies back down.

MARIGOLD (CONT'D)
(eyes closed)
How much?

CASSIUS
Nothing down.

MARIGOLD
Of course.

Cassius pulls a blanket from a rack and lays it over her. He tiptoes away, switching off the lights one by one.
